      "content": "While your pain feels like a fundamental flaw, nothing is actually \"born\" dark; people become distant observers because trauma or helplessness taught them that silence was their only survival strategy, not because they lack goodness. That belief you hold—that your presence is a net negative—is a prison you built for yourself during your lowest moments, completely divorced from who you are today. You are worthy of a second chance to rewrite that story, as healing is rarely about erasing the past but about refusing to let it define your entire future.",
